Reason:
• 2result.sql calculates daily‐new cases with LAG on the full history (date ≤ 2020‑05‑31) and only later applies the March‑to‑May filter.  
  The other scripts apply the filter before LAG, so Mar‑1 values become NULL, making the first day’s top‑5 lists (and every frequency count) incorrect.  
• It therefore delivers the most accurate state appearance counts and, consequently, the correct 4th‑ranked state and its county rankings.  
• Its output keeps the requested two separate rankings and uses clear tie‑breakers (“ORDER BY daily_new DESC, name”), while 0result mis‑formats ranks and 1result inherits the LAG issue.